  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F may be involved in the regulation of HuT78 through a series of target relationships involving T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3. This pathway is supported by multiple independent evidence scores, with Phyllofolactones F acting as a target for CD3, which in turn is targeted by different compounds, including 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, Traxillagenin, and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-. These compounds all ultimately target HuT78, indicating a potential mechanism by which Phyllofolactones F could influence HuT78 through the modulation of CD3. The evidence suggests a possible role for Phyllofolactones F in modulating the activity of CD3, which may then affect HuT78 through downstream signaling pathways. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the different pathways, but the exact mechanism by which Phyllofolactones F interacts with HuT78 remains to be fully elucidated.",
